Find desktop entries and icons through XDG_DATA_DIRS.

applications-rs searches $XDG_DATA_DIRS for desktop entries but forgets the
applications suffix, so nothing is found through them. And it looks for icons
only under the hardcoded /usr/share/icons. On systems where /usr/share is not
populated (like NixOS) that leaves it with almost no applications and no icons.

The patch fixes these problematic behaviours:
  - desktop entries are collected from the $XDG_DATA_DIRS entries themselves
    instead of the applications subdirectory they live in
  - icons are only looked up under /usr/share/icons
  - the icon walk does not follow symlinks
  - icon sizes are parsed from a fixed path component index that only lines up
    for paths as deep as /usr/share/icons

See https://github.com/HuakunShen/applications-rs/pull/18 for a PR to upstream
a more polished version of these changes.

